{"id":"gold_001","question":"What is Dispute Condition 13.1 for merchandise or services not received?","ground_truth":"Dispute Condition 13.1 applies when the cardholder participated in the transaction but the merchandise or services were not received, or the transaction was a cash disbursement that was not received. The merchant has an opportunity to provide proof of delivery or evidence that the cardholder received the merchandise or services.","source_doc":"visa_chargeback_guide","section_hint":"11.10.2 Dispute Condition 13.1","region":"US","type":"lookup","answerable":true,"verified":false,"needs_ground_truth":false}
{"id":"gold_002","question":"What are the rules and caps for daylight overdrafts under the Federal Reserve policy?","ground_truth":"The Federal Reserve PSR policy establishes net debit caps on the maximum amount of daylight overdrafts an institution may incur in its Federal Reserve account. Caps are calculated as a multiple of the institution's capital measure and depend on the institution's cap category (e.g., zero, exempt-from-filing, de minimis, or max cap based on self-assessment).","source_doc":"fed_payment_risk","section_hint":"Daylight Overdrafts","region":"US","type":"lookup","answerable":true,"verified":false,"needs_ground_truth":false}
{"id":"gold_003","question":"What are the requirements for memorized secret authenticators under NIST SP 800-63B?","ground_truth":"Memorized secrets shall be at least 8 characters in length when chosen by the subscriber and at least 6 characters when generated by the CSP. The CSP shall compare memorized secrets against a blacklist of compromised or easily guessable passwords and shall not truncate secrets or impose arbitrary composition rules.","source_doc":"nist_digital_identity_sp800_63b","section_hint":"5.1.1 Memorized Secret Authenticators","region":"US","type":"lookup","answerable":true,"verified":false,"needs_ground_truth":false}
{"id":"gold_004","question":"How do authentication requirements differ between Authenticator Assurance Level 2 and Level 3?","ground_truth":"AAL2 requires multi-factor authentication using either two separate single-factor authenticators or one multi-factor authenticator over an authenticated protected channel. AAL3 requires a cryptographic key stored on a hardware cryptographic authenticator that is verifier-impersonation resistant, meeting FIPS 140 Level 2 overall and Level 3 physical security requirements.","source_doc":"nist_digital_identity_sp800_63b","section_hint":"4.3 Authenticator Assurance Level 3","region":"US","type":"multi_section","answerable":true,"verified":false,"needs_ground_truth":false}
{"id":"gold_005","question":"Under what circumstances is Dispute Condition 10.4 Other Fraud considered invalid for a card-absent environment?","ground_truth":"Dispute Condition 10.4 is invalid if the merchant obtained authorization with an electronic commerce indicator (ECI) indicating 3-D Secure authentication occurred, or if the transaction was processed with an EMV 3-D Secure authentication cryptogram and appropriate liability shift applies.","source_doc":"visa_chargeback_guide","section_hint":"11.7.5.3 Dispute Condition 10.4","region":"US","type":"near_miss","answerable":true,"verified":false,"needs_ground_truth":false}
{"id":"gold_006","question":"Can a subscriber use SMS for authentication at Authenticator Assurance Level 3?","ground_truth":"No, out-of-band authenticators such as SMS or PSTN are not permitted at AAL3. AAL3 mandates a hardware cryptographic authenticator that provides verifier-impersonation resistance.","source_doc":"nist_digital_identity_sp800_63b","section_hint":"5.1.3 Out-of-Band Authenticators","region":"US","type":"paraphrase","answerable":true,"verified":false,"needs_ground_truth":false}
